WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.502
Praise is not payment.

00:00:01.502 --> 00:00:03.379
Purchases beat compliments every time.

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:06.759
This lesson is about interest vs paying demand revisited.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:07.885
Purchases beat praise.

00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:10.513
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.513 --> 00:00:14.268
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.268 --> 00:00:19.900
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.030
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.536
Stay practical: separate feedback from sales before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:30.306
Separate feedback from sales.

00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:32.480
Nice comments go in one column.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.017
Money and booked work go in another.

00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:37.554
Remember the objective: separate feedback from sales.

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:41.540
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.889
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:49.875
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:54.224
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:57.458
Ask for the sale or a paid pilot.

00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:00.008
Interest without a next step is entertainment.

